(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Forty patients with clinically significant periodontal disease underwent randomized) Tj
T*
(allocation to either conventional subgingival instrumentation \(mechanical group, n = 20\)) Tj
T*
(or identical instrumentation supplemented by laser photobiomodulation \(combination group,) Tj
T*
(n = 20\). Periodontal clinical indices improved in both arms over the 5-month observation) Tj
T*
(period; the combination group demonstrated numerically greater gains in gingival health) Tj
T*
(scores \(64% improvement versus 41%, p = 0.06\). Carotid wall hemodynamic assessment) Tj
T*
(revealed divergent trajectories: the combination therapy group exhibited an initial) Tj
T*
(transient 3% decline in shear stress immediately following treatment, followed by) Tj
T*
(sustained 9% elevation at the 20-week timepoint. The mechanical-only group showed minimal) Tj
T*
(net change in arterial hemodynamics across the observation window. Circumferential wall) Tj
T*
(tension and elastic modulus did not differ significantly between groups. These results) Tj
T*
(suggest that photobiomodulation-augmented periodontal care may promote favorable arterial) Tj
T*
(remodeling, potentially contributing to cardiovascular benefit.) Tj
